-- title:
--   Naturality of the variable-change morphism of projective Weierstrass models
-- statement:
--   Let $f : T \to T'$ be a homomorphism of commutative rings, $W$ a Weierstrass curve over $T$ and $C$ a change of variables over $T$, and assume $(C \bullet W).\mathrm{map}\, f = (C.\mathrm{map}\, f) \bullet (W.\mathrm{map}\, f)$. For a Weierstrass curve $V$ over a ring $R$, write $\mathcal O(V)$ for the quotient of $R[X_0,X_1,X_2]$ by the homogeneous ideal generated by the Weierstrass cubic of $V$ in projective form, with the grading `projModelGradingCR` induced from the standard grading, and $\mathrm{Proj}$ of this grading for the projective model. The data are: a graded ring homomorphism $\varphi : \mathcal O(W) \to \mathcal O(C \bullet W)$ with the irrelevant ideal of the target contained in the image of the irrelevant ideal of the source, and satisfying `IsVariableChangeHom`, i.e. $\varphi$ fixes the classes of constants and sends the classes of $X_0, X_1, X_2$ respectively to those of $u^2X_0 + rX_2$, $u^3X_1 + u^2sX_0 + tX_2$ and $X_2$, where $u,r,s,t$ are the components of $C$; a graded homomorphism $\varphi' : \mathcal O(W.\mathrm{map}\,f) \to \mathcal O(C.\mathrm{map}\,f \bullet W.\mathrm{map}\,f)$ with the same two properties relative to $C.\mathrm{map}\, f$; a graded homomorphism $\gamma : \mathcal O(W) \to \mathcal O(W.\mathrm{map}\, f)$, again dominating the irrelevant ideal, with `IsCoefficientHom`, i.e. sending the class of a constant $a$ to that of $f(a)$ and the class of each $X_i$ to the class of $X_i$; and likewise $\gamma_C : \mathcal O(C \bullet W) \to \mathcal O((C \bullet W).\mathrm{map}\, f)$. The conclusion is an equality of morphisms from the projective model of $(C \bullet W).\mathrm{map}\, f$ to that of $W$: $\mathrm{Proj}(\gamma_C)$ followed by $\mathrm{Proj}(\varphi)$ equals the isomorphism $\mathrm{eqToHom}$ coming from the assumed identification of $(C \bullet W).\mathrm{map}\, f$ with $C.\mathrm{map}\, f \bullet W.\mathrm{map}\, f$, followed by $\mathrm{Proj}(\varphi')$ and then $\mathrm{Proj}(\gamma)$.
--
--   This is the compatibility (naturality) of the variable-change morphism between projective Weierstrass models with change of coefficient ring: applying $f$ to the coefficients and then performing the substitution $C.\mathrm{map}\,f$ agrees, on $\mathrm{Proj}$, with performing the substitution $C$ first. It is used in the construction of variable changes realising an isomorphism of Weierstrass models, through [`WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.exists_variableChange_map_fstHom_eq_one_and_smul_eq_of_iso_of_projMap_comp_eq`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.DrinfeldGlobal.exists_variableChange_map_fstHom_eq_one_and_smul_eq_of_iso_of_projMap_comp_eq).
